---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Pricing · Pace"
  description="Pace is free and Apache 2.0. The honest math on what costs money when you adopt it (vendor accounts, Claude plan) and what doesn't (Pace itself, the plugins, the cookbook)."
  canonicalPath="/pricing"
>
  <article class="pricing-page">
    <header class="pricing-header">
      <span class="pricing-eyebrow">Pricing</span>
      <h1>Pace is free.</h1>
      <p class="pricing-lede">
        Pace itself doesn't bill anyone. It's Apache 2.0 open source. You pay for the things you'd pay for anyway: your AI harness subscription and the vendor accounts your team uses.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="pricing-grid">
      <div class="pricing-tier pricing-tier-primary">
        <span class="pricing-tier-label">Free forever</span>
        <h2>Pace itself</h2>
        <div class="pricing-tier-amount">
          <span class="pricing-tier-currency">$</span>
          <span class="pricing-tier-number">0</span>
        </div>
        <p class="pricing-tier-desc">No paywall. No license keys. No "Pro" tier. All 50 plugins. All 11 team guides. The full cookbook. The router.</p>
        <ul class="pricing-tier-includes">
          <li>50 plugins across every team</li>
          <li>Every skill, every connector config</li>
          <li>The <code>/pace</code> router for your company-specific commands</li>
          <li>The cookbook with copy-pasteable recipes</li>
          <li>Self-host or fork freely (Apache 2.0)</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="pricing-tier-cta" href="/docs/install">Install now &nearr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="pricing-tier">
        <span class="pricing-tier-label">Paid by you, not by Pace</span>
        <h2>What costs money</h2>
        <p class="pricing-tier-desc">
          Things you'd be paying for whether Pace existed or not. Pace doesn't take a cut of any of them.
        </p>
        <dl class="pricing-tier-costs">
          <div>
            <dt>Claude subscription</dt>
            <dd>Pro, Max, Team, or Enterprise. Required to run skills in Claude Code or Cowork. <a href="https://claude.com/pricing">Anthropic's pricing</a>.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Routines usage</dt>
            <dd>Cloud-scheduled Routines count against your Claude plan's usage. Free tier exists; heavy automation pushes toward Max / Team.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Vendor accounts</dt>
            <dd>HubSpot, Slack, Snowflake, Notion, Linear, etc. Pace's plugins talk to whatever you already have. We don't resell.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>API costs at the vendor</dt>
            <dd>Some vendors meter API usage (Apollo credits, Snowflake query compute, ZoomInfo lookups). That goes to them, not us.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pricing-section">
      <h2>Optional: GoldenBerry enablement</h2>
      <p>
        We're the small team that maintains Pace. Most companies don't need help : the install, cookbook, and team guides are designed to be self-serve. But if you want hands-on rollout for a 50+ person team (kickoff workshops, role-specific training, custom skill authoring on top of the <code>/pace</code> router, integration with your specific stack), we offer paid enablement.
      </p>
      <p>
        Engagements are project-based, scoped to your team size and tool stack. Email <a href="mailto:hello@goldenberry.so">hello@goldenberry.so</a> to start a conversation. Mention "Pace enablement" in the subject so it routes to the right person.
      </p>
      <p class="pricing-aside">
        We will tell you honestly if a paid engagement isn't a good fit for your situation. Half the conversations end with us pointing you at <a href="/docs/teams">the team guides</a> and saying "you don't need us, this is enough."
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="pricing-section">
      <h2>FAQs</h2>

      <details class="pricing-faq-item">
        <summary>What if Pace becomes popular : will pricing change?</summary>
        <p>
          The router, the plugins, and the cookbook stay free + Apache 2.0. That's a firm commitment of the project. If a future paid surface ever exists (e.g. a hosted analytics layer on top of plugin executions), it would be a separate product, not a license change to what's here today.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="pricing-faq-item">
        <summary>Do I need a Claude subscription specifically?</summary>
        <p>
          To run plugins in Claude Code or Cowork, yes. Pace also installs into Cursor, Gemini CLI, Codex CLI, and 8 other harnesses; in those harnesses you use that harness's pricing. The MCP connector model is harness-agnostic, but Routines (cloud-scheduled execution) are Anthropic-specific.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="pricing-faq-item">
        <summary>What does it cost to install for my 30-person sales team?</summary>
        <p>
          Pace itself: $0. Sales reps need a Claude subscription (Pro starts at ~$20/month). HubSpot/Salesforce/etc. are unchanged from whatever you already pay. If you want Routines firing on a schedule (the Monday pipeline brief), check the <a href="https://claude.com/pricing">Claude plan tiers</a> : Team is usually the right starting point for org-wide automation.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="pricing-faq-item">
        <summary>Are partner plugins (Apollo, Slack, Zoom, etc.) paid?</summary>
        <p>
          The plugin code is free + open source. The vendor service is whatever you pay them today. Apollo charges per credit; Slack/Zoom have their own seat tiers. Pace doesn't change any of that.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="pricing-faq-item">
        <summary>Can I fork Pace and host everything internally?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes. Apache 2.0 license is permissive: fork, white-label, rename the router from <code>/pace</code> to your company name, ship to your own employees. We'd appreciate attribution; not legally required.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .pricing-page {
    max-width: var(--width-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--spacing-xl) var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-3xl);
  }
  .pricing-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .pricing-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .pricing-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .pricing-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .pricing-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .pricing-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .pricing-tier {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-xl);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .pricing-tier-primary {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-paper-elev) 88%, var(--color-forest-dim));
  }
  .pricing-tier-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    align-self: flex-start;
  }
  .pricing-tier h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .pricing-tier-amount {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 4px;
    margin: var(--spacing-xs) 0;
  }
  .pricing-tier-currency {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    color: var(--color-ash);
  }
  .pricing-tier-number {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .pricing-tier-desc {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .pricing-tier-includes {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--spacing-xs) 0 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .pricing-tier-includes li {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    padding-left: 18px;
    position: relative;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .pricing-tier-includes li::before {
    content: '✓';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .pricing-tier-includes code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .pricing-tier-cta {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
    padding: 8px 18px;
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    border-radius: 6px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .pricing-tier-cta:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-hover);
  }
  .pricing-tier-costs {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
    margin: var(--spacing-xs) 0 0 0;
  }
  .pricing-tier-costs > div {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-mist);
    padding-left: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .pricing-tier-costs dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .pricing-tier-costs dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .pricing-tier-costs a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .pricing-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }
  .pricing-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .pricing-section p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .pricing-section a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .pricing-aside {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    font-style: italic;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-mist);
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-left: 2px;
  }
  .pricing-faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    padding: var(--spacing-sm) 0;
  }
  .pricing-faq-item summary {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: var(--spacing-xs) 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .pricing-faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .pricing-faq-item summary::before {
    content: '+';
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-right: var(--spacing-sm);
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .pricing-faq-item[open] summary::before {
    content: '−';
  }
  .pricing-faq-item p {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    padding: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm) 26px;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 7px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
